WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.030
- Well recently, you,

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:03.890
you had a blessing to honor
the spirit of the sunny loss,

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.643
which I think is so beautiful.

00:00:05.643 --> 00:00:06.516
- Thank you

00:00:06.516 --> 00:00:08.760
- I know, I actually
know quite a few people

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.220
who have lost babies and

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.650
had miscarriages and it's one
of those things where half

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.690
the time, like half the time,

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.040
I feel like those friends never
want to talk about it again.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:17.873
- Yes.

00:00:17.873 --> 00:00:19.860
- And then the other
half it's like therapy

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:20.912
for them to talk about it.

00:00:20.912 --> 00:00:21.745
- Yeah

00:00:21.745 --> 00:00:23.475
- It's therapy for them
to remember every year.

00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:24.308
It's, it's so different.

00:00:24.308 --> 00:00:25.820
- Yeah. We're very vocal about it

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.580
in the household because mainly

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.610
because my kids are, you
know, so much a part of it,

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.670
they are, they were part of the blessing.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:33.260
Like, I mean, Miles really sat down

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.610
and paid attention and you know,

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.450
everyone wonders why, you know,

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.200
mommy's crying because of baby Jack.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.653
And, you know, sometimes if I'm just sad

00:00:40.653 --> 00:00:41.980
at just having like a sad night or

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:42.990
a little bit of a down night,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.000
they look at me and they want
to talk about baby Jack and

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.048
they want to talk about,
they'll bring, you know,

00:00:47.048 --> 00:00:50.528
the little box over or the
flowers or, or, you know,

00:00:50.528 --> 00:00:53.300
we, it's, we're just
very vocal about it and

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.660
how he's, you know, he's everywhere.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.810
He's in the air, he's in the sky.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.580
He's, he's surrounds us every day.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:02.580
And I kind of always been like
that, with death and loss,

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:07.880
but yeah, my thing was,
it took me so long to,

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:08.713
you know,

00:01:08.713 --> 00:01:10.160
kind of close the chapter on it.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.430
Of course you never, it's
never like full closure,

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:16.160
but like, I, it happened.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.690
And then I threw myself into this book and

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:24.690
I threw myself into writing and, and.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.610
- For a bit of distraction, you think?

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:27.590
- Yeah, definitely.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:30.860
I mean, that became like,
it became its own thing of,

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.030
and then I looked back one
day and I was like, oh,

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.090
like I just stopped myself.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:38.179
And I was like, oh, I'm
still really sad about this.

00:01:38.179 --> 00:01:39.478
Like it's, I'm like,

00:01:39.478 --> 00:01:42.005
- I think that it is incredible
that you are doing that

00:01:42.005 --> 00:01:44.360
though, because I think a lot
of people feel bad about that.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.240
About still holding and it's
like, that's a horrible loss.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.073
- Yeah

00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:48.906
- That's a huge loss.

00:01:48.906 --> 00:01:50.013
- Yeah

00:01:50.013 --> 00:01:51.700
- And I am opposite of
you. I do not like to talk

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:52.936
about death.

00:01:52.936 --> 00:01:54.690
Like, I am like shut down central.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:55.770
So I think it's an amazing,

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.280
I wish I were more like you with that.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.100
I wish I were more open, like,

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.670
cause I think that a lot of people,

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:01.930
that's how they find healing

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.155
- Yes

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:03.988
- And how a lot of people never heal from.

00:02:03.988 --> 00:02:04.876
- Yeah.

00:02:04.876 --> 00:02:05.709
- Because you don't talk about it.

00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:06.542
- Yeah, it helps a lot.

00:02:06.542 --> 00:02:07.560
And I stuck it in the back of my mind.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.070
And then, and then it, once yeah,

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:14.240
I realized that I remember
looking back and I called my OB

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.060
and I was like, I don't,
this it's been eight months.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.990
And I don't even really
know what went wrong or what

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.340
happened or what to tell
people when we talk about it.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.640
I didn't have any of the answers
for that because I had just

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.601
shut it off for so long.

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:28.510
So really going through everything and,

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.467
and finding peace with it was,

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:34.240
was so big and finding
peace with my entire life.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.900
Like it was such a big, you know,

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:40.100
it was such a big like
sigh, like breath of release

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.760
relief and it just felt,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.220
so it felt so nice the other
day to have the monks there.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.950
And, and

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:47.783
- That's cool.

00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:48.616
- That was great.

00:02:48.616 --> 00:02:49.449
- I think it's really
good for your kids too.

00:02:49.449 --> 00:02:50.840
I don't know if your kids are
already talking about death,

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.610
but my daughter is obsessed
with it and she definitely

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.420
doesn't want me to die.
Every night she tells me.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.253
- Yeah. I get it.

00:02:55.253 --> 00:02:57.050
- But I think it's a hard conversation.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.541
- They do get in that age, right?

00:02:58.541 --> 00:02:59.374
- It's a hard conversation to have.

00:02:59.374 --> 00:03:00.870
So I think what you
are doing is beautiful.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:01.703
What y'all are doing,

00:03:01.703 --> 00:03:03.730
cause it's a beautiful
way to remind your kids.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.020
Like this is life.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:05.853
- Yes

00:03:05.853 --> 00:03:07.100
- Like sometimes death occurs.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.120
Like it's inevitable, for all of us.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.780
- My kids are all about like, talk,

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:10.900
they think I'm going to die all the time

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:11.920
cause of the Disney movies.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.753
So they just.

00:03:12.753 --> 00:03:14.071
- I know

00:03:14.071 --> 00:03:15.840
- Oh my God. And like, anytime
my daughter tells a story,

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.940
everyone dies that could
possibly take care of her.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.210
And I'm like, where is she learning this?

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.750
And I'm like, oh from all
the movies she watches.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.370
- Oh, the stuff I show
her. Oh, yeah that's it.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.203
- All those Disney
films are supposed to be

00:03:25.203 --> 00:03:26.701
like really happy, but it, you should be,

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:29.480
I guess, teaching them, you
know death at some point?

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:30.313
- Yeah. I know.

00:03:30.313 --> 00:03:31.146
Oh, they're prepped for it.

00:03:31.146 --> 00:03:32.170
Thanks Disney.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.720
(laughter)

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:34.553
- So, wait.

00:03:34.553 --> 00:03:36.700
So you spoke about, you
said you weren't drinking.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:37.990
